## 5. What to run next

The next meaningful milestone is not another architecture change. It is a verified live benchmark.

1. Seed a controlled ServiceNow subproduction environment.

2. Verify each seeded defect independently.

3. Run each scenario against its exact target record.

4. Compare the findings with independent ground truth.

5. Repeat the scenarios to measure consistency.

6. Publish recall, precision, false-positive rate, workflow success, recovery rate, and evidence completeness.

## Bottom line

The repository has moved forward structurally, and the LAYA migration has started. But the critical benchmark integrity problems are not fully resolved.

The most important remaining fix is to make the benchmark prove that the agent detected the correct defect on the correct ServiceNow record. Until that works and produces repeatable live results, the evidence-adjusted score remains 4.8/10.
